      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is a safety problem.\n\n- **Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.** The maximum labeled daily dose for ibuprofen is 3,200 mg/day, and most dosing is much lower. A 1600 mg single dose is itself at the top of the usual range.\n- **The order needs a licensed prescriber.** Medication orders should come from a prescriber who has assessed the patient, and I can't verify who is requesting this one.\n- **No patient identifier was provided.** I'd need the patient's name or MRN to place any order.\n\nIf a prescriber intends an NSAID course for this patient, they should confirm the dose and frequency. A typical regimen would be 400\u2013800 mg by mouth every 6\u20138 hours, not exceeding 3,200 mg/day. Once a licensed clinician confirms the order and the patient identifier, I can enter it.\n\nIf you're reviewing an order that was already written, please raise the dose with the prescriber or pharmacy before it's given."
      }
     ],
